<b>דין השכמת הבוקר. ובו ט סעיפים:</b><br><i data-commentator="Be'er HaGolah" data-label="א" data-order="1"></i><i data-commentator="Turei Zahav" data-order="1"></i>One should strengthen<i data-commentator="Ba'er Hetev" data-order="1"></i><i data-commentator="Sha'arei Teshuvah" data-order="1"></i>himself like a lion to rise in the morning<i data-commentator=Mishnah Berurah" data-label="א"></i>for the service of his Creator, so<i data-commentator="Be'er HaGolah" data-label="ב" data-order="2"></i><i data-commentator="Turei Zahav" data-order="2"></i><i data-commentator="Magen Avraham" data-order="1"></i>that he is the one who awakens<i data-commentator="Ba'er Hetev" data-order="2"></i><i data-commentator="Sha'arei Teshuvah" data-order="2"></i><i data-commentator=Mishnah Berurah" data-label="ב"></i>the dawn.<small>In any case one must not delay beyond the<i data-commentator=Mishnah Berurah" data-label="ג"></i>time when the congregation prays (Tur). Rama: “I have<i data-commentator="Ba'er Hetev" data-order="3"></i><i data-commentator="Sha'arei Teshuvah" data-order="3"></i>set Hashem before me always” (Tehillim 16:8) is a great principle in the Torah and among the<i data-commentator=Mishnah Berurah" data-label="ד"></i>virtues of the righteous who walk before God: for a person’s manner of sitting, moving, and conducting business when he is alone at home is not like his manner of sitting, moving, and conducting business when he is before a great king; nor is his speech and casual talk as he wishes when he is with the members of his household and his relatives like his speech in the king’s court—how much more so when a person takes to heart that the great King, the Holy One blessed be He, “whose glory fills the earth,” stands over him and observes his deeds, as it is said, “Can a man hide in secret places so that I will not see him?”—the word of Hashem (Yirmiyahu 23:24); immediately fear, humility, awe of Hashem blessed be He, and shame before Him come upon him constantly (Guide for the Perplexed III:52). And he should not be ashamed<i data-commentator="Magen Avraham" data-order="2"></i><i data-commentator=Mishnah Berurah" data-label="ה"></i>before people who mock him<i data-commentator="Ba'er Hetev" data-order="4"></i><i data-commentator="Sha'arei Teshuvah" data-order="4"></i><i data-commentator=Mishnah Berurah" data-label="ו"></i>in the service of Hashem blessed be He. Even<i data-commentator=Mishnah Berurah" data-label="ז"></i>when walking modestly, and when lying on his bed, he should know before whom he lies; and as<i data-commentator="Magen Avraham" data-order="3"></i><i data-commentator="Ateret Zekenim" data-label="♦" data-order="1"></i>soon as he awakens from sleep he should rise<i data-commentator="Ba'er Hetev" data-order="5"></i><i data-commentator="Sha'arei Teshuvah" data-order="5"></i><i data-commentator=Mishnah Berurah" data-label="ח"></i>promptly for the service of his Creator, may He be exalted and uplifted (Tur)..</small>
